---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Proficiencies"
  description="Frontend engineering capabilities grouped by systems, delivery, quality, and collaboration."
>
  <header class="page-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Capabilities</p>
    <h1>Proficiencies</h1>
    <p>Grouped by the kinds of engineering problems I can help a team reason through.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>Frontend Architecture</h3>
        <p>React, TypeScript, component systems, routing, state boundaries, data fetching, and complex view composition.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>Performance and SSR</h3>
        <p>Server rendering readiness, bundle health, Core Web Vitals, build speed, caching, and runtime measurement.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>Quality and Accessibility</h3>
        <p>Accessible components, test strategy, design system resilience, release checks, and practical frontend reliability.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>Developer Experience</h3>
        <p>TypeScript ergonomics, monorepo workflows, debugging habits, automation, documentation, and review practices.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>Production Operations</h3>
        <p>Rollout strategy, monitoring signals, graceful failure, incident learning, and supportable UI behavior.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>AI-Assisted Engineering</h3>
        <p>LLM-supported debugging, codebase exploration, promptable runbooks, and human-reviewed automation workflows.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
